 "silent_error": "highly_variable_genes with the default flavor='seurat' expects log-normalised input (docstring: 'Expects logarithmized data, except when flavor=seurat_v3/seurat_v3_paper, in which count data is expected'); internally it applies expm1 to undo a log1p. Passing layer='counts' (the layer that seurat_v3 would need) feeds raw counts to the dispersion statistics, which makes the ranking meaningless: in this fixture none of the 12 selected genes is one of the 12 T/B lineage genes, against 7 of 12 when the log-normalised X is used. scanpy emits no warning for this flavor, exit 0, and a plausible list of 12 gene names is written either way.",
